  "construction": "Reversing fold of a pair-partition CPM CSS code of arXiv:2609.30069 with J = 3, L = 8, P = 30. Parent qubit q = c*P + t. Parent X row (j,s) meets c*P + ((s - E[j][c]) mod P) for each block c. The involution is pi(c*P + t) = sigma[c]*P + ((-t - B[sigma[c]]) mod P). Folded site i pairs the i-th smallest q with q < pi(q) with pi(q). Each parent X row becomes one generator, X where it meets a representative and Z where it meets a partner. E = [[26, 28, 2, 13, 16, 11, 0, 13], [6, 17, 10, 29, 22, 9, 18, 24], [10, 18, 7, 16, 14, 18, 4, 0]], sigma = [2, 3, 0, 1, 7, 6, 5, 4], B = [26, 15, 26, 15, 20, 19, 19, 20].",
